# The r19/Acer bug: the rubber-band selection on the desktop left its green outline behind, frame after frame,
# from bottom-left towards top-right. Cause found in flpanel/deskicons.c (the buffer was "cleared" by blending a
# colour of alpha 1 over the old picture). Test: drag rectangles across the desktop through the real pointer; while the
# button is down the band must be visible (pixels), and after the release and a click on an empty spot the screen
# must be what it was before (the clock and the panel are left out). The old build shows the nest of outlines mid-drag
# (picture docs/m7/m20-rubber-r19-middrag.png): the @shotsame inside the band fails there.
@desktop
@wait 4
@shot @OUT@/rb-0-clean.ppm
@drag 80 720 1100 150 @OUT@/rb-1-band.ppm
@wait 2
@shotdiff @OUT@/rb-0-clean.ppm @OUT@/rb-1-band.ppm 400
# the inside of the band, near where the drag started (the old build drew a nest of outlines there): as the clean desktop
@shotsame @OUT@/rb-0-clean.ppm @OUT@/rb-1-band.ppm 60 100 460 400 700
@drag 1150 120 150 650 @OUT@/rb-2-band.ppm
@wait 2
@shotdiff @OUT@/rb-0-clean.ppm @OUT@/rb-2-band.ppm 400
@shotsame @OUT@/rb-0-clean.ppm @OUT@/rb-2-band.ppm 60 850 150 1100 330
@drag 300 300 900 600 @OUT@/rb-3-band.ppm
@wait 2
@mouse 700 450
@click
@wait 3
@mouse 700 300
@wait 2
@shot @OUT@/rb-4-after.ppm
@shotsame @OUT@/rb-0-clean.ppm @OUT@/rb-4-after.ppm 300 0 0 1280 700
